<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phitsanulok</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Phitsanulok is a city on the Nan river in the lower north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>. Under the later Sukhothai kings it became their main seat, and King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borommatrailokkanat">Borommatrailokkanat</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> ruled from it from 1463 to 1488 to direct the wars with Lan Na. Its temple Wat Phra Si Rattana Mahathat houses the revered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phra-phuttha-chinnarat">Phra Phuttha Chinnarat</a> image, and it is the birthplace of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naresuan">Naresuan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/phitsanulok.jpg" alt="Phitsanulok" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Christophe95 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Route_12_in_Phitsanulok_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
